# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .guardrailignore — Pattern exclusions for the slop-intent guardrail scanner
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Format: file glob pattern (matched against relative paths)
# Lines starting with # are comments
# Empty lines are ignored
# Entries are .gitignore-style glob patterns
#
# Usage:
#   bash scripts/guardrail.sh --changed   # skips all entries below
#   bash scripts/guardrail.sh             # skips all entries below
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Test files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files legitimately use test doubles, mocks, and fake data. These are
# excluded because the test framework governs their use, not the guardrail.
__tests__/**
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
*.test.js
*.test.jsx
*.e2e.ts
*.integration.ts

# ── Legacy/vendor code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Code that is not actively being developed — guardrail would create noise.
dist/**
node_modules/**
vendor/**
build/**

# ── Generated code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-generated files may contain stubs that mirror their generator's patterns.
*.generated.ts
*.gen.ts

# ── Configuration and documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────
# These files may reference demo/placeholder terms as *topics*, not code.
*.md
*.yaml
*.yml
*.json
*.json5
*.jsonc
